# The Fuchsia Rust toolchain links the Rust standard library dynamically
# (-Cprefer-dynamic), and libstd has an implicit link attribute on libfdio.so.
# The rustc_*() macros add this to `link_deps` of every Fuchsia Rust
# executable, test and dylib, like GN does with
# //src/lib/fdio/rust:fdio_for_rust_stdlib in BUILDCONFIG.gn.
#
# This is a separate label from //sdk/lib/fdio on purpose. Some Rust targets
# call fdio functions directly and therefore list //sdk/lib/fdio in their own
# `link_deps`. If the macros appended //sdk/lib/fdio itself, those targets would
# end up with the same label twice in `link_deps`, which Bazel rejects with an
# error like:
#
#   Label '//sdk/lib/fdio:fdio' is duplicated in the 'link_deps' attribute of
#   rule 'foo'
#
# The macros cannot simply deduplicate the list, because the label is added
# through a select() whose resolved value is unknown at loading time.
#
# With a distinct alias label, both entries are accepted, and they resolve to
# the same cc_library. Its CcInfo is merged through depsets, so libfdio.so is
# still linked only once.
alias(
    name = "fdio_for_rust_stdlib",
    actual = "//sdk/lib/fdio",
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
